I'm originally from Forfar, Scotland, a small market town twenty minutes from the coast of the North Sea and twenty minutes from the Angus Glens. I always had a creative itch I couldn't quite place.

At nineteen, after a short spell playing professional football for Dundee FC, I moved to the United States on a soccer scholarship at Radford University where I met my wife Fallon during our freshman year. She's from Dandridge, Tennessee, located close to the foothills of the Great Smoky Mountains. We spent our summers and holidays throughout our college years on Douglas Lake or exploring the mountains. Having grown up between the coast and mountains, I fell in love with East Tennessee immediately.
